    "    async def predict(self, pairs: list[tuple[str, str]]) -> list[float]:\n"
), (
    "    async def predict(self, pairs: list[tuple[str, str]], *, background: bool = False) -> list[float]:\n"
), count=15)

# ---- cross_encoder.py: MultiCrossEncoder forwards `background` to its members ----
# v0.9.0's failover chain delegates to member.predict(pairs). The census patch above
# gives MultiCrossEncoder.predict the `background` kwarg, so without this the flag
# would be accepted and then DROPPED on the way to the member that actually owns the
# priority pool — every rerank would enqueue as foreground and #3142's starvation fix
# would be silently dead behind a chain. switchroom runs a single `local` reranker
# today (the chain is only built when HINDSIGHT_API_RERANKER_<n>_* is configured, and
# the secondaries need external API keys we decline), so this is defence-in-depth
# rather than a live path — but a one-line forward is cheaper than the trap.
apply(CE, (
    "                scores = await member.predict(pairs)\n"
), (
    "                scores = await member.predict(pairs, background=background)\n"
), count=1)

